Z||000004||88 Database Nut||02-18-2000||09:37 AM||||While I'm only doing the '88s, there is a guy who is doing ALL years already.  His name is Ray Paulk.  He runs the '88 TTop Registry, and recently started the Indy Registry, but also accepts all years for his database.  Understandably, he receives alot of emails, both Registry related and otherwise, so don't worry if you don't hear back from him right away. I can barely handle the '88 Database, timewise, and can only imagine the work it will take for all the other years.  Please understand, he and I don't mean to offend or exclude owners of other year cars (heck, I've got an 85se onloan to a sister, great car), it's just that I am trying to focus on the last year, that being argueably the most collectible from a low production/ rare option viewpoint.  Ray started with the TTops, another '88 only factory order option.   Now, he's expanded to the Indys and all others too.  Big job. raypaulk@kersur.net<BR>Take Care,  88 Nut with 965 1988 Fieros cataloged.||||reg||7
